From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christophe Pettus <xof@thebuild.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 07:35:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 34/35] H24: refuse a document's CMap stream in hayro-cmap's
 binary format

hayro-cmap parses any CMap data starting with "bcmap" as the binary
format its embedded predefined CMaps are stored in. That parser trusts
its input: it rebuilds each range as previous end + 1 + delta from
Huffman-decoded values (bcmap/mod.rs, six sites), so hostile deltas
overflow. With overflow checks, as in test and fuzz builds, that is a
panic; in release the range wraps and the map is wrong. A /ToUnicode
stream or a Type 0 /Encoding stream reached it straight from the
document.

The format is private to hayro-cmap and legitimately comes only from its
resolver, so is_binary_cmap() now refuses such a stream at both places a
document's CMap is parsed, the same way as a CMap that fails to parse: a
ToUnicode map is absent, a Type 0 font without a usable encoding fails
to load. Predefined CMaps named by the document, the UCS2 fallback and
usecmap still resolve through the bundle and parse as before. hayro-cmap
is not vendored; the gate is the fix until upstream checks the
arithmetic.

Comment-only, in the same patch:
- hayro-jpeg2000: DecodeSettings::resolve_palette_indices no longer
  claims an unresolved multi-component palette image comes back as
  grayscale; it is refused (H16).
- hayro-syntax and hayro-interpret: DecodeLimits::max_image_pixels,
  DecodeFailure::ImagePixelLimit, image_pixel_limit_hits and
  InterpreterWarning::ImagePixelLimit described only the declared-size
  check before any filter; the cap is also checked against each codec's
  header and against the size the codec reports after decoding (H13).
- hayro-syntax jpx.rs: import order and a leading blank line, as rustfmt
  wants them.

The cmap fuzz driver drops "bcmap" input the same way, and the fuzz
reproducer is committed to fuzz/regressions/cmap.

Part of internal #121, #77, #56
